<title>SWEDEN: Handelsbanken seeks wage cost standstill.</title>
<headline>Handelsbanken seeks wage cost standstill.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-10-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's Handelsbanken said it is aiming to keep staff costs at the same absolute level for the next five years.</p>
<p>Managing Director Arne Martensson told a news conference that new systems being introduced to bank offices would cut staff costs by about 15 percent.</p>
<p>The reductions would counter wage increases and lead to unchanged absolute staff costs, he said.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom (46 8 700 1004)</p>
</text>
